    rdfs:label "Evidence for Alkali used in Glassmaking, Pottery & Porcelain: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. GLASS"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The materials of crown glass used to be, fine sand, by measure 5 parts, or by weight 10; ground kelp by measure 11 parts, or by weight 16-1/2; but instead of kelp, soda ash is now generally employed."@en ;
